<title>UK: ING Bank sets $250 million three-year bond.</title>
<headline>ING Bank sets $250 million three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by lead manager Tokyo-Mitsubishi International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ING BANK</p>
<p> AMT    $250 MLN	COUPON     6.125 PCT MATURITY    07.AUG.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.857   PAY DATE    07.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.682    SPREAD	+15 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LUX, AMST PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS **</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  HOLLAND   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  1.175     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.375 PCT MAY 2000 U.S.T</p>
<p> NOTES	DIRECT, UNCONDITIONAL, UNSECURED AND UNSUBORDINATED.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
